## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of approximate quantiles with streaming data, a common constraint in production systems. It compares simple histograms to exact tracking and asks for concrete complexity and error bounds.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming histograms for quantiles
- Per-element O(1) updates, O(W) queries
- Error bounds from bucket width w

## Code Example
```javascript
function HistQuantile(m, W) {
  const bucket = new Array(W).fill(0);
  this.n = 0; this.m = m; this.W = W;
  const w = Math.ceil(m / W);
  this.update = (x) => { const idx = Math.min(Math.floor(x / w), W-1); bucket[idx]++; this.n++; };
  this.median = () => {
    let target = Math.floor(this.n / 2) + 1;
    let cum = 0; let i = 0; const bw = Math.ceil(m / W);
    for (; i < W; i++) { if (cum + bucket[i] >= target) break; cum += bucket[i]; }
    const L = i * bw; const left = target - cum;
    const est = left <= bucket[i] ? L + (left / bucket[i]) * bw : L + bw;
    return est;
  };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adjust for skewed data?  
- How does choosing W affect error vs memory?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to exploit DAG structure for incremental shortest paths with monotone updates and selective recomputation.

## Key Concepts
- DAG topological order
- Monotone updates and lazy propagation
- Selective relaxation focused on targets
- Amortized analysis of edge relaxations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for batch decreases
function applyDecreases(batch) {
  const queue = [];
  for (const e of batch) {
    if (dist[e.v] > dist[e.u] + e.newW) {
      dist[e.v] = dist[e.u] + e.newW;
      queue.push(e.v);
    }
  }
  queue.sort((a,b)=>topo[a]-topo[b]);
  while (queue.length) {
    const x = queue.shift();
    for (const y of adj[x]) {
      const w = weight(x,y);
      if (dist[y] > dist[x] + w) {
        dist[y] = dist[x] + w;
        queue.push(y);
      }
    }
  }
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle dynamic target set changes efficiently?
- What edge cases degrade the amortized bound and how could you mitigate them?

