## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to derive amortized costs for dynamic arrays and relate growth strategies to real hardware effects.

## Key Concepts

- Amortized analysis
- Geometric series and resizing costs
- Growth factor impact on performance
- Cache locality during bulk copies

## Code Example

```javascript
let cap = 1, n = 0, arr = new Array(cap);
function append(x) {
  if (n === cap) {
    const newCap = cap * 2;
    const tmp = new Array(newCap);
    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) tmp[i] = arr[i];
    arr = tmp; cap = newCap;
  }
  arr[n++] = x;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure the actual runtime and memory in a real language? 
- How does adaptive growth (non-constant factor) affect cache misses during resizes?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes real-time top-k maintenance and amortized analysis using simple DS.

## Key Concepts
- HashMap for counts
- Min-heap for top-k
- Tie-breaking rules
- Memory-use trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function update(freq, heap, k, t) {
  freq[t] = (freq[t] || 0) + 1;
  if (heap.has(t)) adjust(heap, t);
  else if (heap.size < k) heap.push([freq[t], t]);
  else if (freq[t] > heap.min()[0]) heap.replace([freq[t], t]);
}
```

